  "worked_solution": "First, notice that $\\frac{3}{2}a$ must be parallel to $a.$\nNow, we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $\\frac{3}{2}a$ is $\\frac{3}{2}$ of the magnitude of $a.$\n\n- Vectors $a$ and $\\frac{3}{2}a$ have the same direction since the factor $\\frac{3}{2}$ is positive.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251575/assets/591682cfbe0f50347d88f894f4c2b740fca140e8a93838f5c53022f9f50ee6da.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
